Please check:
1) the G940 is plugged in and powered;
2) Device Manager lists the G940 (not as an unknown device with a warning icon);
3) the G940 USB cable is connected.

Checking a box, editing a value or a condition writes to disk immediately — there is no “Save” button.
Config file:
{0}

The config could not be written to disk ({0}).
Location: {1}
Common cause: the program sits in Program Files or on a read-only USB drive. Move the whole program folder somewhere writable (for example under Documents). Note: failures to write the alert/button profiles are reported here too.

No HID interface was enumerated on this system.
1) Check that the G940 USB cable is plugged in;
2) The device should appear in Device Manager without a warning mark.

Found {0} HID interfaces, but none of them is the G940 lamp interface (VID {1} / PID {2}).
1) Check that the G940 USB cable is plugged in and Device Manager shows no warning marks;
2) If the name in Device Manager looks right, the PID may differ from the expected one — confirm with the HID probe in “Device diagnostics”.

{0}1) Error 5 (access denied) usually means a standard user was refused — try running as administrator;
2) Error 1 (invalid function) means the report ID or length is wrong — check the feature report list with the “HID probe” first;
3) For other errors, unplug and replug the USB cable once to rule out a driver glitch.
